{"bill":{"id":"119-hr-4619","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"4619","title":"Medicare Mental Health Inpatient Equity Act of 2025","introducedDate":"2025-07-22","latestActionDate":"2025-07-22","latestActionText":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means.","policyArea":"Health","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"T000469","cosponsorBioguideIds":["H001058","D000399","F000466","T000488","B001296","M001224"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"officialSummary":"Medicare Mental Health Inpatient Equity Act of 2025 This bill removes the 190-day lifetime limit on inpatient psychiatric hospital services under Medicare.","congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/4619","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/hr/BILLSTATUS-119hr4619.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:29:46.749Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-hr-4619","plainSummary":"This bill would eliminate the current 190-day lifetime cap on Medicare coverage for inpatient psychiatric hospital care. Under existing law, Medicare beneficiaries can receive only 190 days of inpatient psychiatric services over their entire lifetime; this legislation would remove that limit. The change would allow Medicare beneficiaries with serious mental illness to access inpatient psychiatric treatment without hitting a lifetime ceiling.","industries":[{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"Psychiatric hospitals and inpatient mental health facilities would see expanded Medicare reimbursement eligibility for services beyond the current 190-day cap."},{"industry":"insurance","confidence":0.75,"rationale":"Medicare program costs would increase as the lifetime limit is removed, affecting federal health insurance expenditures and potentially influencing supplemental insurance products."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"c16800581f24eb025853bc48","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:43:07.234Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoe